+# Windows ARM64 Port
+
+Native Windows ARM64 (`aarch64`) support for GNU less 710, as shipped in the
+MSYS2 (`usr/bin`) layer of Git for Windows, on branch `arm64-port`.
+
+The shipped artifact is an MSYS (Cygwin ABI) program, so its ARM64 counterpart
+is built for `aarch64-pc-cygwin` and links the ARM64 `msys-2.0.dll`,
+`msys-ncursesw6.dll` and `msys-pcre2-8-0.dll`. The upstream native-Windows
+MSVC build (`Makefile.wnm`) was also built and checked for ARM64.
+
+## Summary of Changes
+### Build System
+- `Makefile.in`: the `check:` target now passes `CC="${CC}" LDFLAGS="${LDFLAGS}"`
+  to the `lesstest` sub-make. Without this, a cross build (`--host=aarch64-pc-cygwin`)
+  compiled `lesstest`/`lt_screen` with the host x64 gcc while `less_t.exe` was
+  ARM64. Native builds behave the same as before (commit `f485625`).
+- `Makefile.wng`: `MINGW_ROOT_PATH ?=` so an ARM64 mingw prefix (for example
+  `/clangarm64`) can be supplied. The default is unchanged (commit `f485625`).
+
+### Source Code
+- No changes to less itself. There is no SIMD, inline asm, x86 intrinsics or
+  arch `#ifdef` in the code. The `_WIN64` `ssize_t` typedef in `lang.h` is
+  correct for MSVC ARM64. The code was also audited for plain-`char`
+  signedness assumptions (AArch64 GCC uses unsigned `char`) and none were found.
+- `lesstest/pipeline.c` (test harness only): under `#ifdef __CYGWIN__`, PATH is
+  forwarded to the `less_t`/`lt_screen` children. Without it the Windows loader
+  cannot find `msys-2.0.dll` and every lesstest script fails. The x64 MSYS
+  build fails the same way, so this is a Windows/MSYS harness fix that `make check`
+  needs, not an ARM64-specific change (commit `171d2fd`).
+
+### CI/CD
+- `.github/workflows/main.yml`: adds two MSVC ARM64 legs (dist and git sources)
+  on `windows-11-arm`, using `Launch-VsDevShell.ps1 -Arch arm64 -HostArch arm64`.
+  The existing amd64 legs are unchanged, but their check names gain an `amd64` suffix.
+
+### New Files
+- `benchmarks/run_bench.sh`, `benchmarks/base_bench_win_arm.txt`,
+  `benchmarks/base_bench_win_arm.meta.json` (commit `a094bfd`).
+- No vendored SIMD translation libraries.
+
+## Build Steps (ARM64)
+Prerequisites:
+- MSYS2 with the `aarch64-pc-cygwin` cross toolchain (`aarch64-pc-cygwin-gcc`
+  17.0.0) and a sysroot at `/usr/aarch64-pc-cygwin` containing ARM64
+  msys2-runtime, ncurses and pcre2 (headers, import libs and DLLs).
+- `perl`, `make` and `groff` in the MSYS2 shell.
+- For the MSVC build: Visual Studio 2022+ with the **MSVC ARM64 build tools**
+  and the Windows 11 SDK.
+
+### Build (MSYS layer, aarch64-pc-cygwin; same as the MSYS2 PKGBUILD cross arm)
+```sh
+# MSYSTEM=MSYS /c/msys64/usr/bin/bash -l
+cd /c/wos-eval/work/less
+make -f Makefile.aut distfiles
+./configure --build=x86_64-pc-msys --host=aarch64-pc-cygwin --prefix=/usr --sysconfdir=/etc \
+    --with-regex=pcre2 CPPFLAGS=-I/usr/aarch64-pc-cygwin/usr/include LDFLAGS=-L/usr/aarch64-pc-cygwin/usr/lib
+make
+```
+Build output: `less.exe`, `lessecho.exe` in the repo root. Configure chose
+`LIBS = -lncursesw -lpcre2-8`. v710's `all:` target builds no `lesskey`.
+
+### Build (native Windows, MSVC ARM64)
+```bat
+call "C:\Program Files\Microsoft Visual Studio\18\Community\VC\Auxiliary\Build\vcvarsarm64.bat"
+nmake -nologo -f Makefile.wnm generated all
+```
+(`generated` can be skipped when `funcs.h`/`help.c`/`lessmsg.inc` already exist
+from `distfiles`.) Output: `less.exe`.
+
+### Run Tests
+```sh
+# MSYSTEM=MSYS /c/msys64/usr/bin/bash -l   (sysroot bin APPENDED to PATH, not prepended)
+cd /c/wos-eval/work/less
+export PATH=$PATH:/usr/aarch64-pc-cygwin/usr/bin
+make check CC=aarch64-pc-cygwin-gcc VERBOSE=1
+```
+Expected: `RAN  19 tests with 0 errors`.
+
+### Run Benchmarks
+```bat
+C:\msys64\usr\aarch64-pc-cygwin\usr\bin\bash.exe -c "export PATH=/usr/aarch64-pc-cygwin/usr/bin:/usr/bin; cd /c/wos-eval/work; sh less/benchmarks/run_bench.sh arm64-msys /c/wos-eval/work/less/less.exe /c/wos-eval/work/less/less_t.exe /c/wos-eval/work/less-bench-data 7"
+```
+Results are in `benchmarks/base_bench_win_arm.txt`.
+
+## Test Results
+- **Build host**: native ARM64 (Snapdragon X Elite X1E80100, Windows 11 26100)
+- **Executed**: Yes
+- **Upstream suite (`make check`, lesstest)**: Passed 19, Failed 0, Skipped 0.
+  The tests are chinese1, colorbars, filter1, github216, github265, github329,
+  hdr-unicode, hdr-unicode1, osc8-hilite, osc8, proc-special, search-hist,
+  seq200, subsearch, table-50x200, utf8-2.txt, utf8-cmds.txt, version.c and
+  wordwrap. All PASS (`RAN  19 tests with 0 errors`).
+- **Sanity checks**: 20 passed, 0 failed.
+  - Six checks for each of the MSYS and MSVC ARM64 builds (12 results):
+    - README round-trip with `cmp`
+    - `--version` reports PCRE2
+    - 200k-line non-tty paging
+    - `-F` line count
+    - a PCRE2 `+/` search
+    - stdin pipe round-trip
+  - Eight `lessecho` cases, byte-identical to x64 `lessecho`.
+
+## Test Fixes Applied
+- `171d2fd` `lesstest/pipeline.c`: forward PATH to child processes on Cygwin/MSYS.
+  Before the fix, 19/19 tests failed with "error while loading shared libraries"
+  on both ARM64 and x64 MSYS. With it, both pass 19/19.
+
+## Benchmark Results
+- **Result file**: `benchmarks/base_bench_win_arm.txt` (committed on `arm64-port`)
+- **Metadata**: `benchmarks/base_bench_win_arm.meta.json`
+- **Format**: txt
+- **Executed on**: native ARM64 host. The x64 MSYS build was run under Prism
+  emulation for reference.
