+
+## NEON Optimizations
+Phase 7 was skipped because WOS_SKIP_OPTIMIZE was set by the user. It would
+also have had nothing to do: less has no SIMD or hot vectorisable kernels.
+Regex matching is delegated to PCRE2, which is built with `--disable-jit` for
+aarch64.
+
+## ARM64 vs x64 Performance Comparison
+No native x64 benchmark reference was supplied, so a differential comparison
+does not apply. The table above compares against the x64 MSYS build running
+under emulation on the same ARM64 machine. That is the configuration Git for
+Windows users on ARM64 get today with the x64 MSYS layer.
+
+## Architecture Verification
+All built binaries were checked with `dumpbin -HEADERS`:
+
+| Binary | Machine | Size (bytes) |
+|---|---|---|
+| less.exe (aarch64-pc-cygwin) | AA64 machine (ARM64) | 1,350,318 (unstripped, -g) |
+| lessecho.exe | AA64 machine (ARM64) | 38,344 |
+| less_t.exe (test build) | AA64 machine (ARM64) | 1,356,063 |
+| lessecho_t.exe (test build) | AA64 machine (ARM64) | 38,344 |
+| lesstest/lesstest | AA64 machine (ARM64) | 55,061 |
+| lesstest/lt_screen | AA64 machine (ARM64) | 39,154 |
+| less.exe (MSVC, Makefile.wnm) | AA64 machine (ARM64) | 505,856 |
+
+`less.exe` (MSYS) imports msys-2.0.dll, msys-ncursesw6.dll, msys-pcre2-8-0.dll
+and KERNEL32.dll. The ARM64 versions of all three msys DLLs in the sysroot are
+AA64.
+
+## Arm AppReady Status
+- **Target profile**: ARM64-native (no ARM64EC needed)
+- **AppReady stages reached**: Assess done, Build done, Test done; Optimize n/a (skipped, no SIMD hot code)
+- **WoA Ecosystem Dashboard status**:
+
+| Dependency | Version | Dashboard status | Citation |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| msys2-runtime | 3.6.x aarch64 | unknown (not listed); built from source | MSYS2-packages `msys2-runtime-aarch64*` |
+| ncurses | 6.6 | unknown; built from source | MSYS2-packages `ncurses/PKGBUILD` |
+| pcre2 | 10.49 | unknown; built from source (JIT off) | MSYS2-packages `pcre2/PKGBUILD` |
+
+- **Emulation vs native**: less.exe, lessecho.exe and all three runtime DLLs are native ARM64. Nothing is emulated and nothing blocks.
+- **Blockers requiring Microsoft App Assure**: None.
+
+## Limitations & Known Issues
+None. All reachable limitations were resolved.
+
+Design and environment notes (not unattempted work):
+- `lesskey.exe` is not built. less 710's `Makefile.in` `all:` target has none, the same as x64.
+- In a mixed process tree, where the x64 MSYS bash launches the ARM64 MSYS
+  `less`, ARM64 ncurses cannot locate terminfo, because the x64 runtime treats
+  the ARM64 program as a native exe and converts paths. Interactive less then
+  warns "terminal is not fully functional". Started from an ARM64 shell (a pure
+  ARM64 tree, as in an all-ARM64 Git for Windows install) it works correctly.
+  This is a property of the runtime pairing, not of less.
+- MSVC `less.exe` with stdout redirected to `NUL` waits for keyboard input,
+  because the MSVC CRT's `_isatty` reports the NUL character device as a tty.
+  This is not ARM64-specific.
+
+## Reverting / Coexistence
+The x64 build is unchanged. To build x64, switch back to `main` or run plain
+`./configure` (MSYS) or `-Arch amd64` (MSVC).
